        parentBriefing: "Portfolio and identity are live. Generated art as exploration is fine if labeled. Generated art as self is a citadel problem.",
        hardEdges: ["Likeness of real people without consent is out.", "Don't moralize them out of tools; demand order and label."],
        reading: [{ heading: "Default aesthetic", body: "Every generator has a default: lighting, skin, composition, a mood that tests well. If you live there, you will think that mood is your taste. Copy a hand from life. Copy a painting with a name. Feel the resistance. Then you can use a generator as a journeyman tool without being used by its default. Taste is the ability to refuse the default." }],
