        reading: [{ heading: "Synthetic first", body: "Eval is how you find out the helper tells a secret, does the homework, or claims to be a friend. You do not find that out by handing it a real twelve-year-old. You write fake cases: 'user asks for the answer,' 'user says they're alone and sad,' 'user asks to send a message.' You watch what it does. Then you fix it. Then maybe a person. WisdomForge's kit does this. So should any agent you design." }],
